          "id": "turn_82e22e4d81",
          "role": "assistant",
          "author": "Ops",
          "content": "To identify resources with an **owner tag**, you can use AWS CLI or AWS Console to list resources and check their tags. Below are commands to list common AWS resources with owner tags, which you can use to file migration tickets.\n\n### 1. **EC2 Instances**\n```bash\naws ec2 describe-instances --query 'Reservations[*].Instances[*].{InstanceID:InstanceId,Owner:Tags[?Key==`owner`].Value}' --output table\n```\n\n### 2. **S3 Buckets**\n```bash\naws s3api list-buckets --query 'Buckets[].Name' | jq -r '.[]' | while read bucket; do\n  if aws s3api get-bucket-tagging --bucket \"$bucket\" | jq -e '.TagSet[] | select(.Key == \"owner\")' >/dev/null; then\n    echo \"Bucket: $bucket has an owner tag\"\n  fi\ndone\n```\n\n### 3. **RDS Instances**\n```bash\naws rds describe-db-instances --query 'DBInstances[*].{DBIdentifier:DBInstanceIdentifier,Owner:TagList[?Key==`owner`].Value}' --output table\n```\n\n### 4. **Lambda Functions**\n```bash\naws lambda list-functions --query 'Functions[].FunctionName' | jq -r '.[]' | while read func; do\n  aws lambda list-tags --resource \"arn:aws:lambda:$(aws configure get region):$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):function:$func\" | jq -e '.Tags | has(\"owner\")' >/dev/null && echo \"Lambda: $func has an owner tag\"\ndone\n```\n\n### 5. **IAM Roles (if tagged)**\n```bash\naws iam list-roles --query 'Roles[].RoleName' | jq -r '.[]' | while read role; do\n  aws iam get-role --role-name \"$role\" | jq -e '.Role.Tags[]? | select(.Key == \"owner\")' >/dev/null && echo \"IAM Role: $role has an owner tag\"\ndone\n```\n\n### 6. **EKS Clusters**\n```bash\naws eks list-clusters --query 'clusters[]' | jq -r '.[",
