          "role": "assistant",
          "author": "Concierge",
          "content": "As an AI, I don't have a price-match policy since I don't sell products directly. However, many retailers offer price-match guarantees to ensure they remain competitive. Here's a general idea of how price-matching typically works:\n\n1. **Eligibility**: The item must be identical (same brand, model, and specifications) and in stock at the competitor's store or website.\n2. **Proof**: You'll need to provide proof of the competitor's lower price, such as a screenshot, advertisement, or link.\n3. **Timeframe**: Price matches usually need to be requested within a specific time period after purchase (often 7–30 days).\n4. **Exclusions**: Some items, such as refurbished goods, clearance items, or limited-time promotions, may not be eligible.\n\nIf you're considering purchasing the TV, check the retailer's official price-match policy or contact their customer service team for details. They’ll guide you on the process to ensure you get the best deal!",
