          "id": "turn_6a5dd02db4",
          "role": "assistant",
          "author": "Concierge",
          "content": "That’s frustrating! To get this resolved quickly, follow these steps:\n\n### **1. Check Your Bank/Card Statements**  \n- Verify both charges (note the date, amount, and merchant name).  \n- Some issuers may label pending/reversed charges ambiguously—ensure both actually posted.  \n\n### **2. Contact the Subscription Provider**  \n- Reach out to their support via email or live chat (phone if available).  \n- **Script:**  \n  > *\"Hi, I was double-charged for my subscription renewal on [date]. The duplicate charge is [amount] from [merchant name]. Can you confirm if one was an error or process a refund for the duplicate?\"*  \n\n### **3. Dispute the Charge if Needed**  \n- If the provider won’t help, escalate politely:  \n  > *\"If this isn’t resolved, I’ll need to dispute the charge with my bank. Can we fix this today?\"*  \n- Most companies prefer avoiding disputes and will act fast.  \n\n### **4. File a Dispute with Your Bank**  \n- If unresolved, contact your bank/card issuer **immediately**.  \n- Provide screenshots of both charges and any correspondence with the merchant.  \n- Visa/Mastercard rules favor customers in clear duplicate charge cases.  \n\n### **Prevent Future Issues**  \n- Use a virtual card (like Privacy.com) for subscriptions to block accidental renewals.  \n\n**Timeframe**: Refunds typically take 3–10 business days after approval.  \n\nLet me know if you need help drafting an email to the merchant!",
