    "span_id": "span_63916c2e6f",
    "prompt": "I was charged **twice** for the same subscription renewal this month.",
    "response": "I'm sorry to hear about the double charge on your subscription renewal. To resolve this issue effectively, here's a step-by-step approach:\n\n### **1. Check Your Bank/Transaction Records**  \n   - Verify both charges (same amount/subscription name) with your bank or payment method (e.g., credit card, PayPal). Screenshot them for proof.  \n\n### **2. Contact the Subscription Provider**  \n   Reach out to the company’s customer support via:  \n   - **Email**: Look for a billing/refund address or use their contact form.  \n   - **Live Chat/Phone**: Faster resolution (check their website for options).  \n   - **Template Message**:  \n     > *\"Hello, I was charged twice for my subscription renewal on [date] (Transaction IDs: [include if possible]). Please refund the duplicate charge and confirm. Attached are screenshots for reference. Thank you.\"*  \n\n### **3. Dispute the Charge (If Needed)**  \n   If the merchant doesn’t respond or refuses a refund:  \n   - **Credit/Debit Card**: Call your bank to dispute the duplicate charge under \"unauthorized transaction.\"  \n   - **PayPal**: Open a dispute in the Resolution Center.  \n\n### **4. Prevent Future Issues**  \n   - Turn off \"auto-renew\" if possible and monitor future renewals.  \n   - Use virtual cards (e.g., Privacy.com) or prepaid cards for subscriptions.  \n\n### **Example Companies & Direct Links**  \n   - **Netflix**: [Contact Support](https://help.netflix.com/)  \n   - **Spotify**: [Request Refund](https://support.spotify.com/)  \n   - **Apple Subscriptions**: [Report a Problem](https://reportaproblem.apple.com/)  \n\nLet me know the company name if you'd like more tailored steps! For immediate help, their support Twitter/X team often responds quickly to public complaints.  \n\n*\\#Bank reversals are easier within 30 days—act fast!*",
