  "span_60fefa0905": {
    "span_id": "span_60fefa0905",
    "prompt": "Jersey, JE2 postcode. The checkout only offers mainland options.",
    "response": "If you're trying to make an online purchase and the checkout process only offers mainland UK delivery options but not Jersey (JE2 postcode), here are some steps you can take:\n\n### 1. **Check Shipping Policy**\n   - Review the website’s shipping policy to confirm if they ship to Jersey. Some retailers may ship to the Channel Islands but don’t list it as an option during checkout.\n\n### 2. **Contact Customer Support**\n   - Reach out to the retailer’s customer service team via email, live chat, or phone. Provide your JE2 postcode and ask if they can arrange delivery to Jersey.\n\n### 3. **Use a Parcel Forwarding Service**\n   - If the retailer doesn’t ship to Jersey, consider using a UK-based parcel forwarding service. These services provide a UK mainland address for delivery and then forward the package to Jersey.\n\n### 4. **Look for Alternative Retailers**\n   - Some online stores explicitly cater to customers in Jersey or the Channel Islands. Search for retailers that offer shipping to the Channel Islands.\n\n### 5. **Double-Check Your Postcode**\n   - Ensure you’re entering the JE2 postcode correctly. Sometimes, a typo can lead to issues.\n\n### 6. **Use a UK Mainland Address Temporarily**\n   - If you’re unable to resolve the issue and urgently need the item, you could use a UK mainland address (e.g., a friend or family member’s address) and arrange to have it forwarded to Jersey.\n\n### Example Message for Customer Support:\n\"Hi, I’m trying to place an order with the postcode JE2 in Jersey, but the checkout process only allows mainland UK delivery options. Do you ship to Jersey? If so, how can I proceed with my order?\"\n\nLet me know if you'd help drafting a message or finding alternative solutions!",
    "args": null,
    "result": null
  },
