    "prompt": "The on-call pager fired 41 times last night, all from `disk-pressure` warnings.",
    "response": "It sounds like your system experienced significant disk-related issues last night, given the 41 `disk-pressure` alerts. Here’s how to systematically address this:\n\n### 1. **Verify the Current Disk Status**\n   - Check raw disk metrics (not just alerts):\n     ```sh\n     df -h                  # Disk space usage\n     df -i                  # Inode usage (could be a hidden culprit)\n     lsblk                  # List block devices/filesystems\n     ```\n   - For deeper inspection:\n     ```sh\n     sudo iostat -x 5 3     # Disk I/O stats (look for %util >90% or high await)\n     sudo dmesg | grep -i disk  # Kernel logs for disk errors\n     ```\n\n### 2. **Identify the Root Cause**\n   - **Space Issues**:\n     - Locate unexpectedly large files:\n       ```sh\n       sudo du -sh /* 2>/dev/null | sort -h   # Top-level directories\n       sudo du -sh /var/* 2>/dev/null | sort -h  # Common offender (logs, containers)\n       ```\n     - Check log rotation (e.g., for `/var/log`):\n       ```sh\n       ls -lh /var/log/*.log   # Check log file sizes\n       ```\n   - **Inode Issues** (if `df -i` shows 100% usage):\n     ```sh\n     find / -type f | awk -F/ '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -n  # Top dirs by file count\n     ```\n   - **I/O Pressure** (high utilization/latency in `iostat`):\n     - Check for runaway processes:\n       ```sh\n       sudo iotop -o       # Real-time I/O-heavy processes\n       ```\n\n### 3. **Immediate Mitigation**\n   - **Free Space**:\n     - Clear old Docker containers/images (if applicable):\n       ```sh\n       docker system prune -af\n       ```\n     - Delete tmp files older than X days:\n       ```sh\n       find /tmp -type f -mtime +7 -delete\n       ```\n   - **Triage Critical Services**:\n     - Restart services logging excessively (if safe).\n     - Temporarily increase disk space (e.g., expand volume if on cloud).\n\n### 4. **Long-Term Fixes**\n   - **Logging/Monitoring**:\n    ",
