    "prompt": "p95 latency on `/checkout` jumped from 180ms to 900ms at 14:05 UTC.",
    "response": "Here's an analysis of the `/checkout` latency spike:\n\n**Root Cause Analysis**\n1. **Timing Correlation**: \n   - The spike occurred precisely at 14:05 UTC, suggesting a scheduled job/process or deployment\n   - Check if any of these occurred at that time:\n     - Database maintenance (vacuum/analyze, backups)\n     - Cache flushes (Redis/Memcached)\n     - Batch job executions (order processing, analytics)\n\n2. **Recent Changes**:\n   - Check deployment logs - was there a new version rolled out at 14:00 UTC?\n   - Any configuration changes to:\n     - Connection pools (db/cache)\n     - Timeouts\n     - Logging/telemetry levels\n\n3. **Resource Contention**:\n   - Verify CPU/Memory/Disk I/O on database and application servers at 14:05\n   - Network saturation between services?\n\n**Recommended Actions**\n1. **Immediate**:\n   ```bash\n   # Check Kubernetes events if containerized\n   kubectl get events --sort-by=.metadata.creationTimestamp -n checkout\n   \n   # Database locks during incident window\n   SELECT query, wait_event_type, wait_event \n   FROM pg_stat_activity \n   WHERE backend_start > '2024-02-20 14:00:00' \n     AND state = 'active';\n   ```\n\n2. **Forensic**:\n   - Produce flame graphs from application profiling data during the window\n   - Compare EXPLAIN ANALYZE of checkout queries before/during spike\n   - Check for new slow queries in DB logs (log_min_duration_statement)\n\n3. **Prevention**:\n   - Add latency SLO alerts at 300ms for early detection\n   - Implement canary deployments for checkout service\n   - Add critical path tracing (e.g., OpenTelemetry spans for checkout flow)\n\n**Note**: The jump from 180ms → 900ms (5x) suggests either:\n- New serialization delay (DB row locks)\n- Cascading timeouts in downstream services\n- Garbage collection pauses (check GC logs)\n\nWould you like me to draft an incident report template for this event?",
