  "span_8033858ab4": {
    "span_id": "span_8033858ab4",
    "prompt": "Which dashboard shows per-shard cache hit rate?",
    "response": "To find the **per-shard cache hit rate** in Redis, you can check the **Redis Enterprise-specific dashboard** (available in Redis Enterprise Software or Cloud).  \n\n### **Where to Find Per-Shard Cache Hit Rate:**\n1. **Redis Enterprise Web UI / Admin Console**:  \n   - Navigate to **Metrics** or **Performance Analytics**.  \n   - Look for **Cache Hit Rate** metrics, often broken down per shard (especially in clustered deployments).  \n\n2. **Grafana/Prometheus Dashboards (if configured)**:  \n   - A custom Redis Enterprise dashboard (often included in Redis Enterprise monitoring setups) should show **per-shard cache hit rate** in a labeled panel.  \n\n3. **Redis CLI (Command-line)**:  \n   - While not a dashboard, you can check per-shard metrics using:  \n     ```sh\n     redis-cli INFO stats | grep \"keyspace_hits\\|keyspace_misses\"  \n     ```\n   - Calculate hit rate manually: `Hit Rate = keyspace_hits / (keyspace_hits + keyspace_misses)`.  \n\n### **Key Notes:**\n   - **Standard Redis OSS** does not natively expose per-shard cache hit rates—this requires **Redis Enterprise** or manual shard-level metric collection.  \n   - If you're using **Redis Cloud** (managed Redis Enterprise), examine the **Cloud Dashboard**, which provides shard-level granularity.  \n\nWould you like specifics for a particular Redis setup (e.g., AWS ElastiCache, Redis Cloud, self-hosted)? Let me know!",
    "args": null,
    "result": null
  },
